1
00:02:24,911 --> 00:02:26,435
Jay?

2
00:02:28,615 --> 00:02:30,207
Jay, I know this gonna sound strange...

3
00:02:30,283 --> 00:02:34,149
but I don't remember
anything from last night.

4
00:02:37,057 --> 00:02:38,684
Jay?

5
00:02:40,493 --> 00:02:42,154
Jay?

6
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:47,826
Oh, my God.

7
00:02:49,169 --> 00:02:50,898
Oh, my God.

8
00:03:03,750 --> 00:03:05,980
<i>Detective Jay Burgess,
one of the heroes...</i>

9
00:03:06,052 --> 00:03:08,848
<i>from the Charleston
Police Station fire, is dead.</i>

10
00:03:09,022 --> 00:03:12,617
<i>Police apparently received a 911 call
from an unidentified woman...</i>

11
00:03:12,792 --> 00:03:15,022
<i>who spent the night
at Burgess' house.</i>

12
00:03:15,195 --> 00:03:18,653
<i>Police aren't yet saying
if foul play was involved.</i>

13
00:03:18,832 --> 00:03:21,858
<i>We will continue to bring you
more as this story unfolds.</i>

14
00:03:22,035 --> 00:03:24,299
<i>Sue Share for Channel 8 News.</i>

15
00:03:46,459 --> 00:03:48,586
Detective, can you tell me
what happened?

16
00:03:48,762 --> 00:03:50,696
Do you have any idea
how Jay died?

17
00:03:50,864 --> 00:03:54,027
My wife and I watch you
almost every night, Ms. Shelley.

18
00:03:55,835 --> 00:03:56,893
Thank you.

19
00:03:58,772 --> 00:04:04,574
TVN says you're the number one
news reporter in Charleston.

20
00:04:04,744 --> 00:04:09,579
- My, my.
- Yes, I've been very fortunate.

21
00:04:09,749 --> 00:04:10,773
I was asking you...

22
00:04:10,950 --> 00:04:17,287
Truth be told, I'm surprised CNN
or Fox hasn't scooped you up yet.

23
00:04:17,457 --> 00:04:20,893
I bet you end up
on one of those national broadcasts.

24
00:04:21,061 --> 00:04:23,859
Because it's the same
everywhere, isn't it?

25
00:04:24,030 --> 00:04:27,329
It's just easier for people
to hear bad news...

26
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:30,196
when they're looking
at a pretty face.

27
00:04:31,738 --> 00:04:34,866
Look, I'm just trying
to understand here.

28
00:04:35,041 --> 00:04:37,635
Do you think Jay died
from respiratory failure...

29
00:04:37,811 --> 00:04:39,802
or heart attack?

30
00:04:39,979 --> 00:04:43,346
Actually, Ms. Shelley,
we were hoping you could tell us.

31
00:04:43,516 --> 00:04:47,680
This isn't exactly your first brush
with this type of incident, is it?

32
00:04:47,854 --> 00:04:50,789
Sorry, I'm Bill Alexander,
Ms. Shelley's attorney.

33
00:04:50,957 --> 00:04:52,424
Your station manager said...

34
00:04:52,592 --> 00:04:55,117
that I'm at your disposal
as long as you need.

35
00:04:55,295 --> 00:04:56,319
Thank you.

36
00:04:56,496 --> 00:05:00,227
Quite frankly, I was surprised that
Sam thought I needed an attorney...

37
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:04,336
but now I'm actually
glad that he suggested it.

38
00:05:05,672 --> 00:05:08,800
Well, since we're all here...

39
00:05:08,975 --> 00:05:12,138
why don't we go
into the interrogation room.

40
00:05:12,912 --> 00:05:18,282
Just to be clear,
I'm not just giving a statement.

41
00:05:18,451 --> 00:05:21,648
I mean, this is an interrogation...

42
00:05:21,821 --> 00:05:24,346
so you see me
as some sort of suspect.

43
00:05:26,593 --> 00:05:29,118
Well, shall we?

44
00:05:39,472 --> 00:05:41,497
How well did you know
Jay Burgess?

45
00:05:41,674 --> 00:05:44,165
He had given me
a lead on a story, that was it.

46
00:05:44,344 --> 00:05:45,470
When?

47
00:05:45,645 --> 00:05:47,943
Five years ago
right after the fire.

48
00:05:48,114 --> 00:05:50,878
- Were you intimate?
- You don't have to answer that.

49
00:05:51,050 --> 00:05:52,347
No, I wasn't.

50
00:05:52,519 --> 00:05:55,886
- Not until you got the story.
- Again.

51
00:05:56,055 --> 00:05:57,682
No. Not at all.

52
00:05:57,857 --> 00:05:58,983
He did hit on me...

53
00:05:59,159 --> 00:06:02,287
but I heard he was a player
and I just wasn't interested.

54
00:06:02,462 --> 00:06:05,454
- Not that kind of girl?
- That's completely unnecessary.

55
00:06:06,799 --> 00:06:10,098
And then yesterday
out of the blue, he called.

56
00:06:17,243 --> 00:06:19,803
- Britt Shelley.
- Britt, it's Jay Burgess.

57
00:06:19,979 --> 00:06:25,246
Oh, Detective Burgess,
it's been way too long.

58
00:06:25,418 --> 00:06:26,976
Yeah, it has.

59
00:06:27,153 --> 00:06:29,986
<i>Said he had another story for me.
A big one.</i>

60
00:06:30,156 --> 00:06:32,488
<i>But he needed to tell me
about it in person.</i>

61
00:06:32,659 --> 00:06:37,323
My partner on the force, Patty,
passed a few weeks back.

62
00:06:38,498 --> 00:06:41,262
It's hit me hard,
harder than I expected.

63
00:06:41,434 --> 00:06:44,198
I'm sorry to hear that.

64
00:06:44,370 --> 00:06:47,339
It just got me thinking about life
and how short it is...

65
00:06:47,507 --> 00:06:51,170
and, you know, if a man can right
the wrongs that he's done...

66
00:06:51,344 --> 00:06:55,337
well, he should try,
you know, before it's too late.

67
00:07:02,021 --> 00:07:04,353
<i>I don't know
if this means anything or not...</i>

68
00:07:04,524 --> 00:07:07,459
<i>but I remember a man watching us
while we were there.</i>

69
00:07:07,627 --> 00:07:10,596
- Had you ever seen this man before?
- No.

70
00:07:11,364 --> 00:07:14,765
No, I thought maybe he was a fan.

71
00:07:14,934 --> 00:07:16,731
A fan.

72
00:07:16,903 --> 00:07:20,600
Or maybe he recognized Jay
from the police station fire.

73
00:07:20,773 --> 00:07:26,712
Just the way he was looking at us
was so careful not to look at us.

74
00:07:26,879 --> 00:07:28,141
It was strange.

75
00:07:28,581 --> 00:07:32,142
I'm guessing you'll help our sketch
artist come up with a rendering?

76
00:07:32,318 --> 00:07:34,809
- Probably.
- Great.

77
00:07:35,888 --> 00:07:39,153
Mighty convenient, though,
a guy watching you at a bar...

78
00:07:39,325 --> 00:07:42,453
and you happen to notice
and then Burgess happens to die.

79
00:07:42,629 --> 00:07:44,392
You know, I'm a reporter.

80
00:07:44,564 --> 00:07:47,465
That's what I do.
I'm trained to focus on details.

81
00:07:48,835 --> 00:07:51,827
Is that why you left the bar?
Because of this man?

82
00:07:52,005 --> 00:07:53,472
No.

83
00:07:54,407 --> 00:07:56,739
You know what,
straight up, Britt, if...

84
00:07:56,909 --> 00:07:58,968
I prefer to talk about this in private.

85
00:07:59,145 --> 00:08:02,376
Is it all right if we go
to my apartment? It's up the road.

86
00:08:02,548 --> 00:08:04,982
You know what,
all I wanna do is talk.

87
00:08:05,885 --> 00:08:07,853
Scout's honor.

88
00:08:11,291 --> 00:08:14,226
<i>So, what was this big secret?</i>

89
00:08:14,394 --> 00:08:15,418
Okay.

90
00:08:15,595 --> 00:08:19,793
Actually, I never found out.
Everything after that is cloudy.

91
00:08:19,966 --> 00:08:23,595
- What do you mean, cloudy?
- I mean, I don't remember anything.

92
00:08:24,370 --> 00:08:25,928
I can't remember a thing.

93
00:08:26,105 --> 00:08:27,367
You can't remember what?

94
00:08:27,540 --> 00:08:29,804
- Remember taking your clothes off?
- No.

95
00:08:29,976 --> 00:08:31,841
- Getting into his bed?
- No.

96
00:08:32,011 --> 00:08:33,979
So you can't remember having sex?

97
00:08:34,147 --> 00:08:37,139
That's the thing.
I don't know that we did.

98
00:08:37,650 --> 00:08:39,982
I know what it looks like
but I don't think...

99
00:08:40,153 --> 00:08:43,611
Yeah, you weren't interested because
you're not that kind of girl.

100
00:08:43,790 --> 00:08:47,055
All right, I don't think I should
allow my client to continue.

101
00:08:47,226 --> 00:08:50,059
I don't understand
how one glass of wine...

102
00:08:50,229 --> 00:08:52,322
could knock me out like that.

103
00:08:52,498 --> 00:08:55,194
One glass.
It doesn't make any sense.

104
00:09:02,342 --> 00:09:04,037
Wait a minute.

105
00:09:05,712 --> 00:09:07,475
Oh, my God.

106
00:09:08,147 --> 00:09:09,705
The date-rape drug.

107
00:09:10,283 --> 00:09:13,912
The date-rape drug.
That's the only possible explanation.

108
00:09:16,989 --> 00:09:20,390
Okay, I get it that you're playing
the good cop, bad cop thing...

109
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:22,892
but blink if you hear me.

110
00:09:23,062 --> 00:09:26,725
Oh, we hear you, Ms. Shelley.
We hear you fine.

111
00:09:29,302 --> 00:09:32,237
You just don't believe me.

112
00:09:33,639 --> 00:09:35,732
You don't believe me at all.

113
00:09:50,723 --> 00:09:51,747
Look at this.

114
00:09:51,924 --> 00:09:55,758
<i>As the investigation into the death
of Jay Burgess continues...</i>

115
00:09:55,928 --> 00:09:58,089
Not another story about Jay's death.

116
00:09:58,264 --> 00:10:01,495
I know you were big heroes,
but how much more is there to say?

117
00:10:01,667 --> 00:10:02,656
A lot.

118
00:10:02,835 --> 00:10:06,601
The woman he was with
was none other than Britt Shelley.

119
00:10:06,773 --> 00:10:08,900
- From the news?
- Yeah.

120
00:10:09,075 --> 00:10:11,407
<i>Unfortunately
I took a shower this morning...</i>

121
00:10:11,577 --> 00:10:13,977
<i>so we felt it unnecessary
to test for rape.</i>

122
00:10:14,147 --> 00:10:16,445
<i>I have no recollection
of being violated.</i>

123
00:10:16,816 --> 00:10:20,013
<i>- Were you intoxicated, Ms. Shelley?
- No.</i>

124
00:10:20,186 --> 00:10:22,484
<i>I did submit a urine sample
this morning...</i>

125
00:10:22,655 --> 00:10:24,919
<i>to test for so-called
date-rape drugs.</i>

126
00:10:25,091 --> 00:10:28,492
<i>These substances tend to disappear
quickly from the body...</i>

127
00:10:28,661 --> 00:10:32,188
<i>so it's unlikely, at this point,
that anything will be detected.</i>

128
00:10:32,365 --> 00:10:34,890
- She thinks she was drugged?
- I guess so.

129
00:10:35,067 --> 00:10:37,865
You're interested in this
because Jay was your friend?

130
00:10:38,037 --> 00:10:40,665
Or you wish you could
unretire from the force...

131
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:43,104
and solve
this juicy little mystery?

132
00:10:43,276 --> 00:10:45,437
Doing that
would require you to be sober.

133
00:10:45,611 --> 00:10:47,841
Don't start, Miranda.

134
00:10:49,916 --> 00:10:52,783
I can see why
you're so fascinated in all of this.

135
00:10:52,952 --> 00:10:54,943
I mean, the idea of Britt Shelley...

136
00:10:55,121 --> 00:10:57,555
waking up
next to Jay's cold, dead body.

137
00:10:57,723 --> 00:10:59,884
It's not like I care
one way or another...

138
00:11:00,059 --> 00:11:02,653
but you really can't escape
the irony, can you?

139
00:11:02,829 --> 00:11:04,456
No, you can't.

140
00:11:05,865 --> 00:11:08,163
I wonder if Candy's watching.

141
00:11:09,502 --> 00:11:10,526
<i>As Channel 8...</i>

142
00:11:10,703 --> 00:11:11,727
Poor Jay.

143
00:11:11,904 --> 00:11:15,772
<i>Police have not indicated whether
foul play was involved...</i>

144
00:11:15,942 --> 00:11:17,807
Did you know him
when you were a DA?

145
00:11:17,977 --> 00:11:20,946
I knew everyone personally
when I was a DA.

146
00:11:21,113 --> 00:11:25,379
- But Jay and I were friends.
- You're not going to the funeral.

147
00:11:26,118 --> 00:11:29,519
The story is a little sordid.
You don't know where it might lead.

148
00:11:29,689 --> 00:11:33,648
- And with your nomination pending...
- No, no, I won't go to the funeral.

149
00:11:33,826 --> 00:11:36,090
I can't have my name
linked to it right now.

150
00:11:36,262 --> 00:11:38,389
<i>When the coroner
releases his report...</i>

151
00:11:38,564 --> 00:11:41,727
<i>it will help shed some light
on what actually happened.</i>

152
00:11:41,901 --> 00:11:45,166
I wonder if this has to do
with that story she covered...

153
00:11:45,338 --> 00:11:48,000
about the police station fire
five years ago.

154
00:11:48,174 --> 00:11:50,165
Ms. Shelley,
doesn't this remind you...

155
00:11:50,343 --> 00:11:52,402
of the story
that made your career...

156
00:11:52,578 --> 00:11:55,274
about a certain arson investigator,
Raley Gannon?

157
00:11:55,448 --> 00:11:58,576
<i>- There were no drugs in that case.
- There were similarities.</i>

158
00:11:58,751 --> 00:12:02,482
<i>I don't think it's a stretch to say
you buried Mr. Gannon in the media.</i>

159
00:12:02,655 --> 00:12:05,055
If he happens to be watching
this right now...

160
00:12:05,224 --> 00:12:07,988
what do you think
might be going through his head?

161
00:12:10,530 --> 00:12:11,861
<i>There you have it, folks.</i>

162
00:12:12,031 --> 00:12:13,521
<i>The mystery continues...</i>

163
00:12:13,699 --> 00:12:17,066
<i>and we will bring you more
as this story unfolds.</i>

164
00:12:36,422 --> 00:12:38,856
Thank you for sending
that attorney over, Sam.

165
00:12:39,025 --> 00:12:40,287
No problem. Did he help?

166
00:12:40,459 --> 00:12:42,484
<i>He was fine.</i>

167
00:12:42,929 --> 00:12:46,126
I wanted to let you know,
I'm gonna come in to work tomorrow.

168
00:12:46,299 --> 00:12:48,426
Shouldn't you wait
until you feel better?

169
00:12:48,601 --> 00:12:50,125
<i>Come on, you know me.</i>

170
00:12:50,303 --> 00:12:52,897
Work's the only thing
that's gonna make me better.

171
00:12:53,072 --> 00:12:55,506
I would love to have you back
at work tomorrow.

172
00:12:55,675 --> 00:12:57,575
Trust me, we're dying without you.

173
00:12:57,743 --> 00:13:03,204
Hey, you need me and I need
to work so it's a win-win, right?

174
00:13:03,816 --> 00:13:06,649
Yeah, it would be.

175
00:13:06,819 --> 00:13:10,016
Problem is the suits upstairs
have a different take on this.

176
00:13:10,189 --> 00:13:13,920
<i>The public's had their fill of scandal
and the people of Charleston...</i>

177
00:13:14,093 --> 00:13:18,029
<i>might not appreciate
seeing you on TV again so soon.</i>

178
00:13:18,197 --> 00:13:19,221
So, what?

179
00:13:19,398 --> 00:13:23,129
I'm just supposed to sit on my couch
and watch someone else do my job?

180
00:13:23,603 --> 00:13:27,004
Give it a couple of days,
let it shake out. See what's what.

181
00:13:27,173 --> 00:13:28,697
<i>Are you home alone tonight?</i>

182
00:13:28,874 --> 00:13:31,308
You don't have much
in the family department.

183
00:13:31,477 --> 00:13:32,967
But you shouldn't be alone.

184
00:13:33,145 --> 00:13:36,581
Yeah, no, I have a friend over here
taking care of me.

185
00:13:36,749 --> 00:13:39,183
I'm fine, don't worry.

186
00:13:40,019 --> 00:13:41,418
Good night.

187
00:14:32,872 --> 00:14:35,363
- Yeah. Oh, thanks.
- Here you go.

188
00:14:35,541 --> 00:14:38,977
This is the sketch of the guy
she said she saw at the bar.

189
00:14:39,145 --> 00:14:40,703
The phantom stalker.

190
00:14:41,280 --> 00:14:42,770
Right.

191
00:14:46,085 --> 00:14:48,212
Come on,
this guy is totally nondescript.

192
00:14:48,387 --> 00:14:50,412
This could be a picture
of my landlord.

193
00:14:50,589 --> 00:14:53,683
Does she seriously expect us
to believe that's a real guy?

194
00:14:53,859 --> 00:14:55,121
Come on.

195
00:15:03,636 --> 00:15:06,127
Reporter is turning out
to be a pain in the ass.

196
00:15:06,305 --> 00:15:08,739
Thought she'd be too upset
to take a drug test.

197
00:15:08,908 --> 00:15:10,273
Much less go public.

198
00:15:10,443 --> 00:15:14,072
Well, if she's planning
any more surprises...

199
00:15:14,246 --> 00:15:16,646
we'll be the first to know.

200
00:15:29,795 --> 00:15:32,389
Shut up. Get up, get up.

201
00:15:32,565 --> 00:15:33,896
Turn it off!

202
00:15:34,066 --> 00:15:36,330
- I don't know who you are.
- Shut up.

203
00:15:36,502 --> 00:15:39,437
- Shut up and turn it off.
- I don't remember anything.

204
00:15:39,605 --> 00:15:40,731
What are you doing?

205
00:16:13,339 --> 00:16:15,807
Get up. Get up.

206
00:16:22,348 --> 00:16:25,317
- Help!
- Shut up. Shut up.

207
00:16:39,265 --> 00:16:40,630
Raley Gannon?

208
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:43,598
- What are you doing?
- Tell me about Jay Burgess.

209
00:16:43,769 --> 00:16:46,203
- Tell you what?
- What happened last night?

210
00:16:46,372 --> 00:16:48,704
- I have no idea.
- Did you kill him?

211
00:16:48,874 --> 00:16:50,171
- Did I...?
- Did you?

212
00:16:50,342 --> 00:16:52,105
- Are you...?
- Did you kill him?

213
00:16:52,878 --> 00:16:56,575
Did you kill him?

214
00:16:57,249 --> 00:16:59,683
Are you out of your mind?

215
00:17:03,389 --> 00:17:05,880
Look, if you could just loosen up
these ropes...

216
00:17:06,058 --> 00:17:08,993
I will tell you
whatever you want to know.

217
00:17:09,628 --> 00:17:12,529
You think you can bargain with me?
Interesting choice.

218
00:17:12,698 --> 00:17:14,825
Oh, come on,
it's really uncomfortable.

219
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:17,161
Switching tactics.
Expressing frustration.

220
00:17:17,336 --> 00:17:19,827
Do you have any idea
what I have been through?

221
00:17:20,005 --> 00:17:22,803
Attempting to elicit sympathy.
Strategy number three.

222
00:17:23,275 --> 00:17:25,971
Rounding out the performance
with acting defiant.

223
00:17:26,145 --> 00:17:28,636
You ran the victim playbook
in under 60 seconds.

224
00:17:28,814 --> 00:17:30,509
Congratulations.

225
00:17:30,683 --> 00:17:33,550
You get a big A for actress.

226
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:37,348
Cut the crap and answer me.

227
00:17:41,660 --> 00:17:43,685
What do you wanna know?

228
00:17:44,063 --> 00:17:47,965
So, Jave, let's talk motive.

229
00:17:48,667 --> 00:17:53,661
Why does a beautiful,
successful reporter...

230
00:17:53,839 --> 00:17:55,397
kill a playboy cop?

231
00:17:55,574 --> 00:17:58,441
I don't really think
it's all that complicated.

232
00:17:58,611 --> 00:18:02,206
Burgess has a thing for her,
calls her up, asks her out.

233
00:18:02,615 --> 00:18:05,982
Maybe she knows he's a "love them
and leave them" type of guy.

234
00:18:06,151 --> 00:18:07,618
Maybe she doesn't.

235
00:18:07,786 --> 00:18:09,413
Either way, they meet...

236
00:18:09,588 --> 00:18:13,183
he whispers all the right things
in her ear and she falls for it.

237
00:18:13,893 --> 00:18:17,488
Thinks they got some kind
of real connection.

238
00:18:18,731 --> 00:18:23,293
She's a loner so letting him in
emotionally, that's a big freaking deal.

239
00:18:23,836 --> 00:18:26,566
They do the deed
and he goes back to his old self.

240
00:18:26,739 --> 00:18:29,435
Maybe even laughs
at her gullibility.

241
00:18:29,909 --> 00:18:32,434
She's pissed.
She feels totally betrayed.

242
00:18:32,611 --> 00:18:36,547
She snaps. Waits for him
to fall asleep, she kills him.

243
00:18:36,715 --> 00:18:38,080
And she sets it up...

244
00:18:38,250 --> 00:18:40,741
to look like a crime
she once reported on...

245
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:42,820
No, she did that after the fact...

246
00:18:42,988 --> 00:18:46,287
because she figured
it would probably throw us off.

247
00:18:47,359 --> 00:18:50,294
I should've known when I saw
the empty bottle of Scotch.

248
00:18:50,462 --> 00:18:53,260
- It didn't make any sense.
- What didn't make sense?

249
00:18:53,432 --> 00:18:54,490
I hate Scotch...

250
00:18:54,667 --> 00:18:58,626
and I'm not exactly in the habit
of drinking myself into oblivion.

251
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:00,135
I like to be in control.

252
00:19:00,539 --> 00:19:01,801
I believe that.

253
00:19:01,974 --> 00:19:04,636
Why would Jay slip me the drug
at the Wheelhouse...

254
00:19:04,810 --> 00:19:08,177
then make it look like we drank
at the apartment?

255
00:19:08,347 --> 00:19:10,747
Someone else
had to have done it.

256
00:19:12,651 --> 00:19:14,243
All right.

257
00:19:15,020 --> 00:19:16,851
That's enough for now.

258
00:19:17,489 --> 00:19:19,320
I'll sleep on the bed.

259
00:19:19,491 --> 00:19:21,288
You get the floor.

260
00:19:24,063 --> 00:19:26,463
Word of advice,
never look in the direction...

261
00:19:26,632 --> 00:19:29,396
you're gonna strike
before you strike it.

262
00:19:30,135 --> 00:19:33,696
Always follow a kick in the groin
with a shot to the chin.

263
00:19:34,807 --> 00:19:38,971
Not surprising that you know
so much about hand-to-hand combat.

264
00:19:39,411 --> 00:19:41,311
Don't you get
why I brought you here?

265
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:44,210
Because you killed Jay Burgess...

266
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:48,752
and you wanna know how close
the cops are to figuring that out.

267
00:19:51,156 --> 00:19:54,319
I just needed to make sure
that you were telling the truth.

268
00:19:55,694 --> 00:19:58,492
Now I know what happened to you...

269
00:19:58,664 --> 00:20:01,462
and what happened to me
aren't isolated incidents.

270
00:20:02,634 --> 00:20:05,068
- What are you talking about?
- Think it through.

271
00:20:05,237 --> 00:20:08,968
Five years ago, someone arranged
for me to wake up next to a dead body.

272
00:20:09,141 --> 00:20:12,474
Two nights ago, someone
did the exact same thing to you.

273
00:20:13,145 --> 00:20:15,579
I think we were set up
by the same person.

274
00:20:15,748 --> 00:20:20,685
The question is, who and why?

275
00:20:33,532 --> 00:20:35,523
You need some help?

276
00:20:35,701 --> 00:20:37,635
You got it.

277
00:20:39,338 --> 00:20:40,430
I forgot to tell you.

278
00:20:40,606 --> 00:20:45,043
I saw on the news that cop who died,
he was your dad's partner, right?

279
00:20:45,677 --> 00:20:47,975
Yeah, for almost 10 years.

280
00:20:48,147 --> 00:20:51,639
- When was the last time you saw him?
- Jay?

281
00:20:51,817 --> 00:20:53,182
A month ago.

282
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:56,183
Dad's funeral.

283
00:20:58,390 --> 00:21:02,292
He was actually really upset.

284
00:21:02,461 --> 00:21:05,919
You know, it was actually
kind of weird to see him like that.

285
00:21:08,233 --> 00:21:11,168
Listen, honey, I'm not gonna be home
for lunch today.

286
00:21:11,336 --> 00:21:14,999
- You're not working through again?
- I'm afraid so. I'm sorry.

287
00:21:15,941 --> 00:21:17,602
Okay, we're done. All done.

288
00:21:18,644 --> 00:21:20,441
Good job, buddy.

289
00:22:18,704 --> 00:22:20,069
Eggs?

290
00:22:20,239 --> 00:22:24,835
You... You kidnap me,
you interrogate me, and now eggs?

291
00:22:26,712 --> 00:22:27,940
I told you.

292
00:22:28,113 --> 00:22:30,081
I needed to know
what really happened.

293
00:22:30,249 --> 00:22:33,218
- I want to make sure that...
- I was telling the truth.

294
00:22:33,385 --> 00:22:35,046
And now you are.

295
00:22:39,491 --> 00:22:42,289
Fine, don't eat. I don't care.

296
00:22:54,006 --> 00:22:57,169
- The beard's new.
- So?

297
00:22:57,709 --> 00:23:00,473
It suits you. It's very menacing.

298
00:23:04,149 --> 00:23:05,980
I got you some clothes.

299
00:23:06,151 --> 00:23:08,585
Can't have you going to town
dressed like that.

300
00:23:08,754 --> 00:23:10,984
People will get suspicious.

301
00:23:17,796 --> 00:23:20,492
If this kidnapping thing
doesn't work out for you...

302
00:23:20,666 --> 00:23:23,226
you could always become
a personal shopper.

303
00:23:26,905 --> 00:23:29,669
You thought what happened to you
five years ago...

304
00:23:29,841 --> 00:23:33,174
and what happened to me
the other night were somehow related.

305
00:23:33,745 --> 00:23:35,144
Our stories are similar.

306
00:23:35,314 --> 00:23:37,748
Especially considering
they both involve Jay.

307
00:23:38,050 --> 00:23:39,847
Charleston's a very small town.

308
00:23:40,018 --> 00:23:42,009
Jay knew everybody,
everybody knew Jay.

309
00:23:42,187 --> 00:23:45,748
So it's not surprising he could've
been involved in both situations.

310
00:23:45,924 --> 00:23:49,485
Second of all,
only one element is really the same.

311
00:23:49,661 --> 00:23:51,822
We both woke up
next to a dead body.

312
00:23:53,999 --> 00:23:56,934
That's a pretty big one element,
don't you think?

313
00:23:57,869 --> 00:24:01,737
I will admit there is that one
glaring similarity...

314
00:24:01,907 --> 00:24:04,432
but all the other circumstances
are different.

315
00:24:04,610 --> 00:24:06,942
You got drunk
and had sex with a drug addict.

316
00:24:07,112 --> 00:24:09,273
Nobody slipped you anything
in your drink.

317
00:24:09,448 --> 00:24:12,542
Actually, I always suspected
that somebody did.

318
00:24:12,718 --> 00:24:15,585
- Don't look at me like that.
- This is the way I look...

319
00:24:15,754 --> 00:24:18,621
when someone tells a story
that strains credibility.

320
00:24:18,790 --> 00:24:21,190
I don't care. That's what happened.

321
00:24:21,360 --> 00:24:23,385
Someone slipped you
the date-rape drug?

322
00:24:23,562 --> 00:24:26,588
Apparently,
it's not just for women anymore.

323
00:24:28,867 --> 00:24:30,698
Okay. Who?

324
00:24:31,870 --> 00:24:34,395
Yeah, well,
that's where it gets complicated.

325
00:24:36,475 --> 00:24:38,238
I'm listening.

326
00:24:40,145 --> 00:24:41,703
Okay.

327
00:24:42,080 --> 00:24:43,515
The police station fire.

328
00:24:52,324 --> 00:24:55,020
- Candy, are you all right?
- I'm fine, Jay, I'm okay.

329
00:25:01,166 --> 00:25:02,428
Help her.

330
00:25:03,268 --> 00:25:05,429
- Ground floor's clear.
- The basement?

331
00:25:05,604 --> 00:25:06,901
I don't know.

332
00:25:07,072 --> 00:25:09,768
- George?
- All right, we better check.

333
00:25:09,941 --> 00:25:12,273
- You can't go back there.
- Candy, stay here.

334
00:25:12,444 --> 00:25:13,843
Pat, let's go.

335
00:25:25,590 --> 00:25:28,081
- Raley.
- Get out of here. Get back, okay?

336
00:25:28,260 --> 00:25:30,319
Jay, George and Pat
went back in there.

337
00:25:30,495 --> 00:25:32,725
We got three cops inside.

338
00:25:33,332 --> 00:25:34,799
Bring him out. Let's go.

339
00:25:34,966 --> 00:25:37,434
Bring him out.
Put him on the ground.

340
00:25:37,602 --> 00:25:40,127
Easy, easy. Is he breathing, Jay?

341
00:25:40,305 --> 00:25:42,796
- I don't think he's breathing.
- Get out of here.

342
00:25:42,974 --> 00:25:44,965
Pat, Jay, get out of here.

343
00:25:58,990 --> 00:26:01,151
<i>I was the investigator in charge.</i>

344
00:26:01,326 --> 00:26:03,920
<i>All the evidence suggested
that Cleveland Jones...</i>

345
00:26:04,096 --> 00:26:07,429
<i>the one fatality,
had actually set the fire.</i>

346
00:26:07,599 --> 00:26:09,533
Seemed like just desserts.

347
00:26:09,701 --> 00:26:11,896
I just had a few loose ends
to wrap up.

348
00:26:12,070 --> 00:26:13,162
It wasn't my story...

349
00:26:13,338 --> 00:26:17,104
but I do remember my boss waited
a while for that arson report.

350
00:26:17,275 --> 00:26:20,176
Yeah, because I was waiting on Jay.

351
00:26:20,345 --> 00:26:23,143
Come on, Jay, I came all the way
down here to get it.

352
00:26:23,315 --> 00:26:25,681
- Yeah, I know, man.
- I can't do the report...

353
00:26:25,851 --> 00:26:30,083
until I finish the investigation.
I can't finish until I get the Jones file.

354
00:26:30,255 --> 00:26:33,452
Look at this place.
I can't even find a frigging pen.

355
00:26:33,625 --> 00:26:36,856
His autopsy said cause of death
was actually a skull fracture.

356
00:26:37,028 --> 00:26:40,327
I'm not clear whether he got
that before or after the fire.

357
00:26:40,499 --> 00:26:42,364
- Any idea?
- He didn't get it before.

358
00:26:42,534 --> 00:26:45,230
Maybe he hit his head
when he was trying to get out.

359
00:26:45,404 --> 00:26:47,565
Really, man, who cares, you know?

360
00:26:47,739 --> 00:26:50,264
I mean, the guy
was in a revolving door to juvie.

361
00:26:50,442 --> 00:26:53,843
- I mean, armed robbery, assault.
- But not arson.

362
00:26:54,012 --> 00:26:56,071
He learned a new trick
at juvenile hall.

363
00:26:56,248 --> 00:26:58,944
I just need this file
and then I can close the case.

364
00:26:59,117 --> 00:27:01,449
Raley, I know you're trying
to do your job.

365
00:27:01,620 --> 00:27:03,713
I'm trying to get out of here early.

366
00:27:03,889 --> 00:27:05,584
- Yeah, I know. Your party.
- Yeah.

367
00:27:05,757 --> 00:27:08,123
This place
that I'm house-sitting, it's huge.

368
00:27:08,293 --> 00:27:10,853
It's worth it to come by
to see this monstrosity.

369
00:27:11,029 --> 00:27:13,554
- Jay, I can't.
- Everybody's gonna be there.

370
00:27:13,732 --> 00:27:14,858
George, Pat, Candy.

371
00:27:15,033 --> 00:27:17,467
- It's that Haley's got this thing...
- Bring her.

372
00:27:17,636 --> 00:27:19,001
I can't. She's going away.

373
00:27:19,171 --> 00:27:21,696
She's going to visit her sister.
I told you that.

374
00:27:21,873 --> 00:27:23,135
Yeah, I just forgot.

375
00:27:23,308 --> 00:27:26,505
It's perfect, though. Why don't you
just come by for a drink?

376
00:27:26,678 --> 00:27:28,908
I tell you what,
you come by for a drink...

377
00:27:29,080 --> 00:27:32,277
I will find the file,
I will bring it to the fire house...

378
00:27:32,451 --> 00:27:34,885
first thing in the morning.
What do you say?

379
00:27:35,053 --> 00:27:37,044
- You're gonna bring it to me?
- Yeah.

380
00:27:38,089 --> 00:27:40,353
Why do you care so much
if I come?

381
00:27:40,525 --> 00:27:45,986
It's just, you know, since the fire,
I'm feeling a little sentimental.

382
00:27:46,164 --> 00:27:49,133
Might be kind of nice
to have the whole gang together.

383
00:27:52,137 --> 00:27:54,367
- Okay.
- All right.

384
00:27:56,174 --> 00:27:58,699
- I'll see you later.
- Hey, can you pick up Candy?

385
00:27:58,877 --> 00:27:59,901
She needs a lift.

386
00:28:00,078 --> 00:28:02,205
Always something with you,
isn't it?

387
00:28:02,380 --> 00:28:03,745
- See you.
- Yeah.

388
00:28:04,749 --> 00:28:06,478
You look good, Raley. Happy.

389
00:28:06,651 --> 00:28:09,552
Do I? I guess I am.

390
00:28:09,721 --> 00:28:11,655
You look good too. New dress?

391
00:28:11,823 --> 00:28:14,018
Not any newer
than last time you saw it.

392
00:28:14,593 --> 00:28:18,393
- You lost weight?
- Ten pounds, actually.

393
00:28:18,997 --> 00:28:23,127
Yep, another one
of Jay's free-for-alls.

394
00:28:33,578 --> 00:28:36,547
Don't play with your food,
just drink it.

395
00:28:36,715 --> 00:28:38,239
They'll let anybody in there.

396
00:28:38,416 --> 00:28:40,043
- George.
- Hey, glad you made it.

397
00:28:40,218 --> 00:28:43,346
Hey, Pat.
Hey, where's our gracious host?

398
00:28:43,522 --> 00:28:46,320
Jay's right over there.
Where do you think?

399
00:28:49,194 --> 00:28:51,094
- Well, I'm empty. Raley?
- No, thanks.

400
00:28:51,263 --> 00:28:54,164
- Suit yourself.
- I'll take one.

401
00:28:54,332 --> 00:28:56,266
I'm down with that.

402
00:29:15,086 --> 00:29:17,748
Your friend thought
you might like this.

403
00:29:19,090 --> 00:29:22,924
I hear you're a fireman.
I like firemen.

404
00:29:23,428 --> 00:29:28,798
Look, thanks for the drink,
but I'm engaged.

405
00:29:28,967 --> 00:29:30,559
Oh, yeah?

406
00:29:31,036 --> 00:29:32,367
Are you sure?

407
00:29:34,406 --> 00:29:38,843
That's not usually the response
I get, but yeah, I'm sure.

408
00:29:39,010 --> 00:29:41,376
Last week I priced out minivans.

409
00:29:42,314 --> 00:29:43,679
I got it.

410
00:29:43,848 --> 00:29:46,476
But there's no reason
why we can't talk, is there?

411
00:29:46,651 --> 00:29:49,882
I mean, at least take the drink.

412
00:29:57,529 --> 00:29:59,190
Cheers.

413
00:30:10,909 --> 00:30:15,846
So the girl who walked out
on the terrace, you didn't know her?

414
00:30:16,448 --> 00:30:18,814
Never seen her before in my life.

415
00:30:19,985 --> 00:30:22,510
- And she turned out to be a...
- Yeah.

416
00:30:24,055 --> 00:30:25,283
Yeah.

417
00:30:29,060 --> 00:30:31,051
I never knew that she pursued you.

418
00:30:32,130 --> 00:30:34,291
You never knew a lot of things.

419
00:30:40,138 --> 00:30:41,833
Okay, so she gave you a drink...

420
00:30:42,007 --> 00:30:44,840
you took a couple of sips,
and then what?

421
00:30:45,010 --> 00:30:47,945
And then I have no idea.

422
00:30:49,514 --> 00:30:51,778
<i>The next morning I woke up...</i>

423
00:30:52,817 --> 00:30:54,444
<i>we were naked...</i>

424
00:30:55,987 --> 00:30:57,978
<i>and she was dead.</i>

425
00:30:58,823 --> 00:31:00,882
I found Jay.

426
00:31:05,363 --> 00:31:07,797
<i>Since we were kids,
Jay was able to think fast.</i>

427
00:31:07,966 --> 00:31:10,196
She's a junkie,
nobody's gonna miss her.

428
00:31:10,368 --> 00:31:13,337
- You know this girl?
- Yeah, I've seen her around.

429
00:31:14,539 --> 00:31:18,373
Hey, be cool, don't worry about it.
We're gonna take care of it.

430
00:31:18,543 --> 00:31:22,070
<i>And he promised me that everything
was gonna be just fine.</i>

431
00:31:23,281 --> 00:31:26,682
I just woke up next to a dead body
and Jay Burgess promised me...

432
00:31:26,851 --> 00:31:30,082
that everything
was gonna be just fine.

433
00:31:31,056 --> 00:31:32,489
Yeah, but I don't get it.

434
00:31:32,657 --> 00:31:35,148
Why didn't you include this
in your statement...

435
00:31:35,326 --> 00:31:37,658
that you thought
somebody had drugged you?

436
00:31:37,829 --> 00:31:39,888
I wanted to.
Candy convinced me not to.

437
00:31:40,065 --> 00:31:41,089
Candy?

438
00:31:41,266 --> 00:31:45,726
Okay, just to be clear, we're
talking about Cassandra Mellers...

439
00:31:45,904 --> 00:31:47,667
who's about to be confirmed...

440
00:31:47,839 --> 00:31:50,706
as the youngest female
federal judge in the country?

441
00:31:50,875 --> 00:31:53,935
Yeah, we called her Candy.
She's an old friend.

442
00:31:54,112 --> 00:31:57,445
Yeah, at the time she was
the Charleston DA. Talking to you...

443
00:31:57,615 --> 00:32:00,209
Would've seriously jeopardized
her career. I know.

444
00:32:00,385 --> 00:32:02,182
We'd always relied on each other.

445
00:32:02,353 --> 00:32:04,787
I'm telling you, I don't remember.

446
00:32:04,956 --> 00:32:06,924
She must've put something
in my drink.

447
00:32:07,092 --> 00:32:10,653
That may be true but the problem is
it will be hard to verify.

448
00:32:10,829 --> 00:32:12,922
Then I'll take a drug test.

449
00:32:13,565 --> 00:32:16,830
Look, Raley, say you were drugged.

450
00:32:17,001 --> 00:32:18,901
Chances
of the date-rape substance...

451
00:32:19,070 --> 00:32:21,504
remaining in your system
this long are slim.

452
00:32:21,673 --> 00:32:24,164
By asking, you're casting suspicion
on yourself.

453
00:32:24,342 --> 00:32:26,367
You're admitting
you don't remember...

454
00:32:26,544 --> 00:32:28,136
- what happened.
- I don't.

455
00:32:28,313 --> 00:32:32,181
Which will make people wonder
if you have something to hide.

456
00:32:32,851 --> 00:32:35,820
Now, look at it the other way.

457
00:32:35,987 --> 00:32:38,353
Say you don't ask for the test.

458
00:32:38,823 --> 00:32:42,691
In the meantime, the girl’s death
is ruled an accidental overdose.

459
00:32:42,861 --> 00:32:46,058
That's it. It's over.

460
00:32:46,231 --> 00:32:47,892
You'll be in the clear.

461
00:32:49,501 --> 00:32:51,526
I know, I know.

462
00:32:55,573 --> 00:32:57,700
I wish it were different.

463
00:32:58,343 --> 00:33:01,107
You know, this story,
it wasn't originally my beat.

464
00:33:01,279 --> 00:33:04,942
But then I started investigating
and Pat Wickham, George McGowan...

465
00:33:05,116 --> 00:33:06,378
no one told me this.

466
00:33:06,551 --> 00:33:07,882
You don't believe me?

467
00:33:08,753 --> 00:33:12,587
Not like I give a damn what you think.
Because you have moral standards.

468
00:33:12,757 --> 00:33:15,453
- What is that supposed to mean?
- I came clean fast.

469
00:33:15,627 --> 00:33:19,085
Pat and George made sure the
investigation stayed under the radar.

470
00:33:19,264 --> 00:33:21,926
My life might've actually
gotten back on track.

471
00:33:22,100 --> 00:33:24,000
Until ace reporter Britt Shelley...

472
00:33:24,169 --> 00:33:28,003
decided to build a career
on my story.

473
00:33:28,173 --> 00:33:30,835
<i>Things get worse for
fire inspector Raley Gannon...</i>

474
00:33:31,009 --> 00:33:33,876
<i>as pressure mounts
for his resignation.</i>

475
00:33:34,045 --> 00:33:36,309
<i>Police are questioning
Gannon's coworkers...</i>

476
00:33:36,481 --> 00:33:38,972
<i>in connection with the death
of Suzi Monroe.</i>

477
00:33:39,150 --> 00:33:41,380
<i>The coroner has not
released his report.</i>

478
00:33:41,553 --> 00:33:45,080
<i>Mr. Gannon remains the only person
of interest in this case.</i>

479
00:33:50,829 --> 00:33:52,387
Get dressed.

480
00:33:55,767 --> 00:33:58,429
Ms. Shelley, this is Bill Alexander,
your attorney.

481
00:33:58,603 --> 00:34:02,130
This is the third time I've tried
to reach you this morning.

482
00:34:02,307 --> 00:34:03,433
The police called.

483
00:34:03,608 --> 00:34:06,133
The coroner's office
is going to announce...

484
00:34:06,311 --> 00:34:09,246
Jay Burgess' cause of death,
and when that happens...

485
00:34:09,414 --> 00:34:11,143
they may want to speak to you.

486
00:34:11,316 --> 00:34:13,978
Would you please call me
and tell me where you are?

487
00:34:14,152 --> 00:34:15,176
Thanks.

488
00:34:23,127 --> 00:34:24,754
- George.
- What?

489
00:34:24,929 --> 00:34:26,920
- You have company.
- Hi, Miranda.

490
00:34:27,098 --> 00:34:29,089
What are you doing here, Pat?

491
00:34:29,267 --> 00:34:32,566
Can we make this quick, please?
We have to be at the club.

492
00:34:33,171 --> 00:34:34,468
I'll meet you there.

493
00:34:37,141 --> 00:34:39,166
George, we need to talk.

494
00:34:39,777 --> 00:34:41,540
What are you so jumpy about, Pat?

495
00:34:41,713 --> 00:34:45,706
Jay's gone and nobody gives a damn
about your little secret.

496
00:34:45,884 --> 00:34:48,512
You do, George.
If you don't, you really should.

497
00:34:48,686 --> 00:34:49,846
Get a grip.

498
00:34:50,021 --> 00:34:52,080
Britt Shelley's attorney
can't find her.

499
00:34:52,257 --> 00:34:53,656
I bet she skipped town.

500
00:34:54,158 --> 00:34:57,559
Think about it. She's a reporter,
she thinks someone drugged her.

501
00:34:57,729 --> 00:34:59,594
She'll start
to put things together.

502
00:34:59,764 --> 00:35:02,733
Things about me, things about you.

503
00:35:04,969 --> 00:35:06,630
George?

504
00:35:13,645 --> 00:35:15,112
Yeah.

505
00:35:15,546 --> 00:35:18,310
Okay, thank you.

506
00:35:19,417 --> 00:35:21,351
Britt Shelley's tox report.

507
00:35:21,519 --> 00:35:24,249
No date-rape drug.
Surprise, surprise.

508
00:35:24,422 --> 00:35:26,356
We gotta find this woman, man.

509
00:35:26,524 --> 00:35:29,687
- She lies, she bails.
- She kills.

510
00:35:29,861 --> 00:35:32,830
I just heard from the coroner.

511
00:35:32,997 --> 00:35:34,487
You called it.

512
00:35:34,666 --> 00:35:38,932
Jay Burgess got drunk and
someone smothered him in his sleep.

513
00:35:39,103 --> 00:35:42,903
This case
is now officially a homicide.

514
00:35:46,277 --> 00:35:48,905
- Take my car back to Charleston.
- What?

515
00:35:50,248 --> 00:35:52,239
I'll figure out how to pick it up.

516
00:35:52,417 --> 00:35:54,749
Come on, let's go.
You gotta get out of here.

517
00:35:56,688 --> 00:36:00,419
Fine. But for the record,
you have no right to blame me.

518
00:36:00,591 --> 00:36:02,286
For following the wrong story...

519
00:36:02,460 --> 00:36:05,759
- or screwing up my life?
- What do you mean, the wrong story?

520
00:36:06,531 --> 00:36:09,091
You know what,
all the evidence pointed to you.

521
00:36:09,267 --> 00:36:11,394
I will not apologize
for doing my job.

522
00:36:11,569 --> 00:36:13,298
You accused me of murder.

523
00:36:13,471 --> 00:36:16,531
When the autopsy came back,
I reported it was an overdose.

524
00:36:16,708 --> 00:36:19,973
It didn't matter.
By then nobody trusted me anymore.

525
00:36:20,778 --> 00:36:23,611
You're not just talking
about your coworkers, are you?

526
00:36:24,649 --> 00:36:27,243
- You're talking about that girl.
- Haley.

527
00:36:27,418 --> 00:36:29,409
I tried to get an interview
with her...

528
00:36:29,587 --> 00:36:32,818
We weren't just dating.
We were engaged.

529
00:36:34,425 --> 00:36:36,620
Raley, I got a lead
and I followed it.

530
00:36:36,794 --> 00:36:38,591
Exactly.

531
00:36:38,763 --> 00:36:40,958
And who gave you that lead?

532
00:36:42,133 --> 00:36:45,899
Five years ago, Jay did, right?
Mr. Everything's Gonna Be Fine.

533
00:36:46,070 --> 00:36:47,662
That is how I first met him.

534
00:36:47,839 --> 00:36:50,774
He came to me with your story
and told me he was sure...

535
00:36:50,942 --> 00:36:52,807
you killed that girl.

536
00:36:52,977 --> 00:36:56,378
- How did you know that I met him?
- Don't you get it?

537
00:36:56,547 --> 00:36:58,742
Don't you see
the big picture here?

538
00:36:59,584 --> 00:37:01,882
I've had five years
to put this together.

539
00:37:02,053 --> 00:37:04,021
I've looked at it from every angle...

540
00:37:04,188 --> 00:37:06,713
and along the way,
I found out a few things.

541
00:37:06,891 --> 00:37:09,985
One, the party house,
it didn't belong to any friend.

542
00:37:10,161 --> 00:37:13,494
<i>Jay rented it under a fake name
so it couldn't be traced to him.</i>

543
00:37:13,664 --> 00:37:18,658
<i>Two, the girl, Jay had known
she was a drug addict for years.</i>

544
00:37:19,170 --> 00:37:21,468
And three,
after realizing one and two...

545
00:37:21,639 --> 00:37:24,665
it seemed obvious that Jay
must have contacted you.

546
00:37:24,842 --> 00:37:27,811
My point being
that you missed the real story.

547
00:37:27,979 --> 00:37:32,507
That Jay Burgess
carefully orchestrated all of it.

548
00:37:32,884 --> 00:37:35,114
Getting you
to blast my face on the news...

549
00:37:35,286 --> 00:37:37,413
was just the final nail
in the coffin.

550
00:37:37,588 --> 00:37:40,113
It just... It doesn't make sense.

551
00:37:40,291 --> 00:37:43,385
I mean, why would he try
to screw up your career...

552
00:37:43,561 --> 00:37:46,052
and risk ruining his own?

553
00:37:48,533 --> 00:37:51,093
That's exactly
what I wanted to know.

554
00:37:51,269 --> 00:37:53,203
And I could only think of one thing.

555
00:37:54,372 --> 00:37:55,999
The Cleveland Jones file.

556
00:38:11,089 --> 00:38:13,250
What do you think
would be in that file...

557
00:38:13,424 --> 00:38:15,392
that could possibly
be so terrible?

558
00:38:15,560 --> 00:38:17,187
I wish I could tell you.

559
00:38:17,695 --> 00:38:20,095
After I lost my job,
the arson investigator...

560
00:38:20,264 --> 00:38:22,824
that took over the case closed it.

561
00:38:23,334 --> 00:38:25,461
If he did get
the Cleveland Jones file...

562
00:38:25,636 --> 00:38:27,900
he didn't include it
in the final report.

563
00:38:29,207 --> 00:38:34,941
And then he bought a car
and a new house...

564
00:38:35,113 --> 00:38:37,479
and took his wife
on a cruise to Mexico.

565
00:38:37,648 --> 00:38:40,446
- So you think Jay paid him off?
- Someone did.

566
00:38:40,618 --> 00:38:43,212
Until yesterday,
I always thought Jay acted alone.

567
00:38:43,387 --> 00:38:46,356
Then it hit me that Jay
must have had an accomplice.

568
00:38:46,524 --> 00:38:48,219
And that accomplice killed him...

569
00:38:48,392 --> 00:38:51,452
Because he was gonna finally
tell me the truth.

570
00:38:52,663 --> 00:38:55,188
- Do you have a phone?
- No.

571
00:38:55,366 --> 00:38:57,300
Of course not.

572
00:38:57,702 --> 00:38:59,169
You do.

573
00:39:02,140 --> 00:39:03,573
You took my purse?

574
00:39:03,741 --> 00:39:06,266
Needed to make it look
like you left on your own.

575
00:39:06,444 --> 00:39:09,936
Good. That will go over well
with the cops since they love me.

576
00:39:10,114 --> 00:39:11,672
Who are you calling?

577
00:39:11,849 --> 00:39:15,250
Well, if I was following
the wrong story...

578
00:39:15,419 --> 00:39:18,547
maybe it's not too late
for me to get the right one.

579
00:39:20,358 --> 00:39:21,552
<i>Hi, Sam, it's me.</i>

580
00:39:21,726 --> 00:39:24,923
- Britt, where are you?
- I didn't skip town.

581
00:39:25,096 --> 00:39:27,621
<i>I don't think you understand
how serious this is.</i>

582
00:39:27,798 --> 00:39:32,030
Oh, yeah, no, I do, I do.
I'm trying to get to the bottom of it.

583
00:39:32,203 --> 00:39:34,899
<i>- It's about the police station fire.
- What about it?</i>

584
00:39:35,072 --> 00:39:36,699
<i>I don't have the details yet...</i>

585
00:39:36,874 --> 00:39:39,342
<i>but Jay Burgess' death
relates back to it.</i>

586
00:39:39,944 --> 00:39:42,640
<i>- And you know this how?
- I'm gonna need your help.</i>

587
00:39:42,813 --> 00:39:46,579
<i>Track down the paperwork on Jones,
the guy that started the fire.</i>

588
00:39:47,985 --> 00:39:52,012
<i>Don't bother looking at the fire
investigation report. It's not there.</i>

589
00:39:52,790 --> 00:39:54,621
<i>Okay, listen to me, Britt.</i>

590
00:39:54,792 --> 00:39:57,556
Sam, you gotta trust me on this.
This is really good.

591
00:39:57,728 --> 00:40:00,561
I'm gonna save my ass.
I'm gonna break open a story.

592
00:40:00,731 --> 00:40:02,699
Yeah, from where? Jail?

593
00:40:02,867 --> 00:40:05,358
Coroner's report came.
Jay Burgess was murdered.

594
00:40:05,536 --> 00:40:06,798
It's official.

595
00:40:06,971 --> 00:40:10,236
<i>They've actually issued
a warrant for your arrest.</i>

596
00:40:10,408 --> 00:40:12,842
<i>You gotta turn yourself in.</i>

597
00:40:14,045 --> 00:40:16,445
<i>Britt, are you listening to me?</i>

598
00:40:17,615 --> 00:40:20,209
<i>Yeah. Yeah, I heard you.</i>

599
00:40:20,384 --> 00:40:23,410
- You got her?
- Got her.

600
00:40:24,589 --> 00:40:27,786
You'll want these. Directions.

601
00:40:27,959 --> 00:40:29,927
I don't understand
why you won't come.

602
00:40:30,094 --> 00:40:33,222
What happened to me is confirmation
of what happened to you.

603
00:40:33,397 --> 00:40:35,627
- If we go to the police...
- You kidding?

604
00:40:35,800 --> 00:40:39,133
I don't trust the cops anymore.
I sure as hell don't trust you.

605
00:40:39,303 --> 00:40:43,137
You destroyed my life. You think I'd
give you the chance to do it again?

606
00:40:43,307 --> 00:40:45,002
I listened to your story.

607
00:40:45,176 --> 00:40:46,939
You have selective memory.

608
00:40:47,111 --> 00:40:50,410
Back when I was reporting on you
I begged you for an interview.

609
00:40:50,581 --> 00:40:53,812
I gave you the opportunity
to tell your side but you wouldn't.

610
00:40:53,985 --> 00:40:55,213
- Shut up.
- No.

611
00:40:55,386 --> 00:40:57,354
You lay low and let things pass by.

612
00:40:57,521 --> 00:41:00,422
- Just shut up.
- No, you should've fought back.

613
00:41:01,292 --> 00:41:04,489
You should've fought.
If not for yourself, for your fiancée.

614
00:41:04,662 --> 00:41:07,529
You have no idea
how much I wanted to fight for her.

615
00:41:07,698 --> 00:41:08,926
No idea.

616
00:41:14,905 --> 00:41:17,237
Raley, I'm sorry.

617
00:41:17,775 --> 00:41:19,265
I'm sorry.

618
00:41:24,682 --> 00:41:27,446
I know exactly why I'm alone.

619
00:41:29,086 --> 00:41:30,553
What's your excuse?

620
00:44:39,443 --> 00:44:40,876
Damn it!

621
00:45:00,831 --> 00:45:02,230
It's okay.

622
00:45:11,041 --> 00:45:13,976
So are you guys close
to catching her?

623
00:45:17,181 --> 00:45:19,046
I mean, Jay was my dad's partner...

624
00:45:19,216 --> 00:45:22,447
so he was kind of like a father
to me himself.

625
00:45:26,290 --> 00:45:30,056
Yeah, we understand. Really.

626
00:45:30,227 --> 00:45:31,854
We got an APB out on her.

627
00:45:32,029 --> 00:45:35,260
- Every cop in the state is on high alert.
- Great.

628
00:45:36,433 --> 00:45:37,457
Good.

629
00:45:41,472 --> 00:45:44,964
You know, she comes across
as very earnest and innocent...

630
00:45:45,142 --> 00:45:50,876
but my father always told me that
those were the most dangerous type.

631
00:45:55,953 --> 00:45:57,113
Just that...

632
00:46:00,457 --> 00:46:01,947
Okay.

633
00:46:27,518 --> 00:46:29,247
Are you okay?

634
00:46:31,488 --> 00:46:34,889
I should take you to the hospital,
I think you're still in shock.

635
00:46:35,326 --> 00:46:36,657
No.

636
00:46:36,827 --> 00:46:39,819
I'm fine, it's just a little cut.

637
00:46:55,045 --> 00:46:56,774
Guessing you couldn't see who...

638
00:46:56,947 --> 00:47:00,041
Two men, black Mercedes,
that's all I could tell.

639
00:47:00,217 --> 00:47:03,744
Your station manager, you think
maybe his phone was bugged?

640
00:47:03,921 --> 00:47:05,684
Not his, probably mine.

641
00:47:07,491 --> 00:47:11,518
The fact someone knows I'm looking
for the Jones file and tried to kill me...

642
00:47:11,695 --> 00:47:13,219
means we're getting close.

643
00:47:13,397 --> 00:47:16,662
Those guys after you
think you're dead. Works in our favor.

644
00:47:16,834 --> 00:47:19,701
Gotta be another way
to figure out what's in that file.

645
00:47:21,472 --> 00:47:23,372
It's okay.

646
00:47:25,309 --> 00:47:27,300
I'm sorry. I'm...

647
00:47:30,047 --> 00:47:31,674
I...

648
00:47:32,016 --> 00:47:34,644
I just need a minute.

649
00:48:39,049 --> 00:48:40,539
Britt?

650
00:48:44,354 --> 00:48:45,787
Britt?

651
00:49:43,480 --> 00:49:45,448
- Hey, Raley?
- Yeah?

652
00:49:50,053 --> 00:49:51,884
Less menacing?

653
00:49:53,390 --> 00:49:54,823
What?

654
00:49:54,992 --> 00:49:56,619
You going somewhere?

655
00:49:56,794 --> 00:49:58,853
Yeah, Jay's funeral.

656
00:50:01,131 --> 00:50:04,464
Well, I was thinking we've been going
about this the wrong way.

657
00:50:04,935 --> 00:50:05,959
What do you mean?

658
00:50:06,136 --> 00:50:09,537
There must be someone who knows
what was going on with Cleveland.

659
00:50:09,706 --> 00:50:12,038
He must have been close
to somebody.

660
00:50:37,201 --> 00:50:39,396
So why don't you let me
ask the questions?

661
00:50:39,570 --> 00:50:40,594
Why?

662
00:50:40,771 --> 00:50:44,605
You're sure he'll open up if you
woo him with your wily feminine ways?

663
00:50:44,775 --> 00:50:49,337
No, I'm a good reporter and collecting
information is what I do for a living.

664
00:50:49,513 --> 00:50:52,744
Thank you so much for that
backhanded, sexist non-compliment.

665
00:50:57,888 --> 00:50:58,946
Can't you read?

666
00:50:59,122 --> 00:51:01,283
Mr. Jones,
you probably don't remember me.

667
00:51:01,458 --> 00:51:04,985
Met years ago. I was investigating
the fire that killed your son.

668
00:51:05,162 --> 00:51:06,595
I remember you.

669
00:51:07,164 --> 00:51:10,156
Like I said then, he set it, he died...

670
00:51:10,334 --> 00:51:14,361
and sometimes justice
has a way of taking care of itself.

671
00:51:14,771 --> 00:51:18,764
- We're not sure that's what happened.
- Either way, the boy died.

672
00:51:19,176 --> 00:51:20,871
We're not sure that he had to.

673
00:51:25,215 --> 00:51:27,706
I'm Britt Shelley, news reporter.

674
00:51:27,885 --> 00:51:29,614
I know who you are.

675
00:51:29,786 --> 00:51:31,777
I got a TV.

676
00:51:31,955 --> 00:51:36,415
Right now it's telling me you're the one
that killed that hero policeman.

677
00:51:36,593 --> 00:51:38,686
All the more reason
I need your help.

678
00:51:39,029 --> 00:51:41,657
I believe someone's trying
to frame me for murder.

679
00:51:41,832 --> 00:51:44,858
They think I know a secret
about your son's death.

680
00:51:45,035 --> 00:51:48,027
Send me away and neither of us
will find out what it is.

681
00:51:52,743 --> 00:51:55,837
It can't be easy. Losing a child.

682
00:51:56,013 --> 00:51:58,641
Cleveland was no child.

683
00:51:59,049 --> 00:52:03,145
I couldn't keep up with all the times
that boy was in and out of jail.

684
00:52:03,320 --> 00:52:05,185
Rape, robbery.

685
00:52:05,355 --> 00:52:08,552
Pretty sure
he had his very own personal cell.

686
00:52:09,459 --> 00:52:13,919
Last time I saw him I told him
I wasn't gonna bail him out no more.

687
00:52:14,097 --> 00:52:18,295
Next thing I get a call from the police
telling me he was dead.

688
00:52:20,237 --> 00:52:22,501
What was the name
of the officer who called?

689
00:52:22,673 --> 00:52:24,368
I don't remember.

690
00:52:24,541 --> 00:52:26,975
You must have been in shock.

691
00:52:27,377 --> 00:52:29,038
Not really.

692
00:52:29,846 --> 00:52:31,973
Sure wish I got back the lighter,
though.

693
00:52:32,149 --> 00:52:35,414
Cleveland really loved that thing.

694
00:52:35,852 --> 00:52:37,911
- The lighter?
- Yeah.

695
00:52:38,088 --> 00:52:40,056
My daddy bought it for him.

696
00:52:40,223 --> 00:52:42,191
It had this...

697
00:52:42,359 --> 00:52:47,956
This picture on it of a half-naked girl,
she was, like, wearing a...

698
00:52:48,131 --> 00:52:50,599
What was it? A red bikini.

699
00:52:52,402 --> 00:52:57,169
Every time Cleveland saw that thing
he would... He would laugh.

700
00:52:57,341 --> 00:52:59,901
Didn't come back with his stuff,
though.

701
00:53:01,178 --> 00:53:05,581
I asked the cops about it
and they said they never saw it.

702
00:53:07,784 --> 00:53:11,447
The day that your son died,
he was arrested.

703
00:53:11,621 --> 00:53:12,747
Do you know what for?

704
00:53:14,091 --> 00:53:15,922
I don't know.

705
00:53:16,259 --> 00:53:19,490
He used to like to hang out
with his loser friends...

706
00:53:19,663 --> 00:53:22,496
down in Hampton Parkway.

707
00:53:22,933 --> 00:53:27,063
I wouldn't be surprised
if they got him defacing property.

708
00:53:27,571 --> 00:53:31,564
- What about the skull fracture?
- What?

709
00:53:33,477 --> 00:53:36,002
Skull fracture. Didn't they tell you?

710
00:53:45,922 --> 00:53:49,949
So the question is, how did Cleveland
get the skull fracture?

711
00:53:50,127 --> 00:53:52,721
Why didn't the cops tell his father?

712
00:53:53,230 --> 00:53:54,424
Who interrogated him?

713
00:53:55,032 --> 00:53:56,226
Jay, George and Pat.

714
00:53:56,400 --> 00:53:59,062
They claimed he was fine
when he left the room.

715
00:53:59,236 --> 00:54:01,966
The next thing they know
the station was on fire.

716
00:54:02,639 --> 00:54:03,867
Well, Jay's dead.

717
00:54:04,041 --> 00:54:07,272
Pat Wickham died a couple
months ago, that leaves George.

718
00:54:07,444 --> 00:54:09,139
Most likely suspect.

719
00:54:09,312 --> 00:54:11,246
How'd he know
Jay was gonna come clean?

720
00:54:11,415 --> 00:54:14,316
Well, I'll be sure to ask him.
I gotta get going.

721
00:54:16,219 --> 00:54:18,483
Hey, I'm gonna do a little research.

722
00:54:18,655 --> 00:54:20,953
I saw a computer in the motel office.

723
00:54:21,658 --> 00:54:23,455
Are you kidding?

724
00:54:24,227 --> 00:54:26,491
You're not going.
There's a warrant out.

725
00:54:26,663 --> 00:54:29,427
The last thing you need to be doing
is hanging out.

726
00:54:29,599 --> 00:54:32,659
So? You want me to sit here
and watch television all day?

727
00:54:32,836 --> 00:54:35,134
That's why we got a room
with cable.

728
00:54:52,722 --> 00:54:56,326
Can you clear my schedule?
I've decided to go to Jay's funeral.

729
00:55:13,276 --> 00:55:16,837
Left, left, left.

730
00:55:17,013 --> 00:55:20,176
God bless
and peace be with all of you.

731
00:55:25,055 --> 00:55:27,489
Thank you.
It was a beautiful service.

732
00:55:28,525 --> 00:55:31,119
- Miss you around the station.
- Thanks for coming.

733
00:55:31,294 --> 00:55:33,694
- Coming from Atlanta, I hear.
- Yeah.

734
00:55:35,365 --> 00:55:36,389
George.

735
00:55:38,001 --> 00:55:39,935
Raley.

736
00:55:48,778 --> 00:55:50,473
It's good to see you.

737
00:55:50,647 --> 00:55:52,706
I was so hoping you'd be here.

738
00:55:53,150 --> 00:55:57,314
- Candy, I'm so sorry about Jay.
- Me too.

739
00:55:58,321 --> 00:56:02,223
I missed you. I tried to find you,
but you didn't leave much of a trail.

740
00:56:02,392 --> 00:56:05,418
I just needed
not to be found for a while.

741
00:56:05,595 --> 00:56:08,029
- Congratulations on the nomination.
- Thank you.

742
00:56:08,198 --> 00:56:09,563
I can't say I'm surprised.

743
00:56:10,333 --> 00:56:11,766
It means a lot to me.

744
00:56:11,935 --> 00:56:13,402
Judge Mellers.

745
00:56:13,570 --> 00:56:16,061
Forgive me,
but you do have another appointment.

746
00:56:16,473 --> 00:56:19,636
- I'm sorry, Raley, I have to...
- It's okay.

747
00:56:21,645 --> 00:56:24,307
I know this may not be the time
or the place...

748
00:56:24,481 --> 00:56:28,577
but I'm not gonna get another
chance and it's always bothered me.

749
00:56:28,752 --> 00:56:30,276
After Suzi Monroe died...

750
00:56:30,754 --> 00:56:35,919
maybe I didn't advise you well
about the drug test.

751
00:56:36,693 --> 00:56:38,126
Maybe...

752
00:56:40,030 --> 00:56:41,224
Maybe I made a mistake.

753
00:56:43,600 --> 00:56:49,436
If you need anything...
I mean it, anything.

754
00:56:49,606 --> 00:56:51,267
Thank you.

755
00:56:51,808 --> 00:56:53,275
Take care.

756
00:56:55,779 --> 00:56:57,269
Raley.

757
00:56:57,781 --> 00:57:00,079
- George McGowan.
- It's been a while.

758
00:57:00,250 --> 00:57:04,346
Jay would've appreciated
that you came out of hiding for this.

759
00:57:04,788 --> 00:57:06,380
No doubt.

760
00:57:07,490 --> 00:57:11,324
- I heard you've been doing well lately.
- I fell in love.

761
00:57:11,494 --> 00:57:14,088
With a woman? Or money?

762
00:57:18,335 --> 00:57:23,363
Well, I guess that the marriage
didn't exactly work out as I planned.

763
00:57:23,540 --> 00:57:25,269
Too bad.

764
00:57:25,442 --> 00:57:28,138
Add one more thing
to your list of regrets, huh?

765
00:57:28,311 --> 00:57:30,006
Something on your mind, Raley?

766
00:57:30,647 --> 00:57:34,014
Yeah, there is. Jay's murder.

767
00:58:07,050 --> 00:58:08,415
May I help you, ma'am?

768
00:58:08,585 --> 00:58:11,247
Yeah, I was wondering
if I could use your computer.

769
00:58:11,421 --> 00:58:14,788
Actually we have an entire
business center set up right there.

770
00:58:14,958 --> 00:58:16,448
Thanks.

771
00:58:16,626 --> 00:58:19,356
You might need to plug it in first.

772
00:58:22,999 --> 00:58:24,990
I don't know any more than you do.

773
00:58:25,168 --> 00:58:29,161
Apparently, that newswoman killed
him after they got back from the bar.

774
00:58:29,339 --> 00:58:32,331
He met her at a bar?
I don't remember that in the news.

775
00:58:32,509 --> 00:58:34,943
He told me he was going to do it.

776
00:58:35,111 --> 00:58:38,706
He was thinking of retiring, gonna
convince her to do a story on him.

777
00:58:38,882 --> 00:58:40,474
- That really why?
- Yeah.

778
00:58:40,650 --> 00:58:43,050
Or did he want to
get something off his chest?

779
00:58:43,219 --> 00:58:44,550
Like what?

780
00:59:49,219 --> 00:59:50,811
Hey, Pat.

781
00:59:51,588 --> 00:59:53,112
Come here.

782
01:00:00,997 --> 01:00:05,559
Do you have any idea what Jay
might've wanted to tell a reporter?

783
01:00:06,469 --> 01:00:09,700
No, no. I have no clue.

784
01:00:16,413 --> 01:00:17,846
Hey.

785
01:00:19,916 --> 01:00:21,850
Let's see.

786
01:00:22,852 --> 01:00:25,150
Fried shrimp.

787
01:00:26,189 --> 01:00:28,589
And... And salad?

788
01:00:28,758 --> 01:00:29,816
That's what you got?

789
01:00:29,993 --> 01:00:33,053
- I thought you'd want...
- Fried shrimp, good call.

790
01:00:33,730 --> 01:00:35,994
- So did you talk to George?
- Yeah.

791
01:00:36,166 --> 01:00:39,192
George and Pat Jr. looked
like they had something to hide.

792
01:00:39,369 --> 01:00:43,533
Well, you may not be wrong.
Read that.

793
01:00:43,706 --> 01:00:46,732
- What, you went out?
- Oh, come on, just read it.

794
01:00:47,544 --> 01:00:51,674
It says here that five years ago
in Hampton Park...

795
01:00:51,848 --> 01:00:54,078
Pat Wickham Jr. was attacked.

796
01:00:54,250 --> 01:00:58,584
Must've been how he got the scar. His
dad said he got it in some bar brawl.

797
01:00:59,155 --> 01:01:01,453
The kid never seemed like the type.

798
01:01:01,891 --> 01:01:06,089
And Hampton Park, that's where
Cleveland Jones used to hang out.

799
01:01:06,262 --> 01:01:07,456
Some coincidence.

800
01:01:07,630 --> 01:01:10,030
So you think
we should go talk to Pat Jr.?

801
01:01:10,200 --> 01:01:11,292
Absolutely.

802
01:01:11,468 --> 01:01:13,766
God, I always hated that park.

803
01:01:13,937 --> 01:01:16,371
Full of dealers and junkies.

804
01:01:16,539 --> 01:01:18,769
Haley cut through there
on her morning run.

805
01:01:19,209 --> 01:01:21,769
I begged her to find another route.

806
01:01:24,214 --> 01:01:30,380
You know, I've actually been meaning
to say something to you about that. I...

807
01:01:31,054 --> 01:01:35,184
I realized that my story is what caused
you to lose that relationship with her.

808
01:01:35,358 --> 01:01:36,950
And I just...

809
01:01:37,126 --> 01:01:40,357
I just want you to know
that I am truly, truly sorry.

810
01:01:41,831 --> 01:01:46,962
Yeah, well, I guess I've been telling
myself that for the past five years.

811
01:01:47,136 --> 01:01:48,797
That it was all your fault.

812
01:01:48,972 --> 01:01:51,099
If you hadn't kept my face
in the news...

813
01:01:51,274 --> 01:01:53,640
there wouldn't have been
so much pressure.

814
01:01:53,810 --> 01:01:57,337
And she and I,
we would've been okay.

815
01:01:58,181 --> 01:02:02,743
Truth is, I know it's not that simple.

816
01:02:02,919 --> 01:02:06,320
You know,
you said that I should've fought.

817
01:02:06,489 --> 01:02:10,983
- If not for myself then for my fiancée.
- Raley, I should...

818
01:02:11,160 --> 01:02:15,722
The thing is, it was Haley
who begged me not to fight.

819
01:02:16,099 --> 01:02:19,626
She wanted it
to just all go away on its own.

820
01:02:21,271 --> 01:02:22,966
What did you want?

821
01:02:23,406 --> 01:02:25,601
I wanted her to stay.

822
01:02:26,743 --> 01:02:28,802
I wanted to make her happy.

823
01:02:30,847 --> 01:02:32,712
And she left anyway.

824
01:02:32,882 --> 01:02:34,816
She couldn't stick it out.

825
01:02:35,718 --> 01:02:37,743
She wasn't like you.

826
01:02:38,388 --> 01:02:40,413
She wasn't a fighter.

827
01:03:33,142 --> 01:03:35,235
Yeah, got it.

828
01:03:36,913 --> 01:03:41,282
All right, Raley Gannon just surfaced
at Jay Burgess' funeral.

829
01:03:47,523 --> 01:03:51,323
- Any idea where he'll turn up next?
- Yeah, boss gave me an address.

830
01:03:53,363 --> 01:03:56,594
Well, judge,
I have to say it's an honor to meet you.

831
01:03:56,766 --> 01:04:00,395
I think the whole city is excited
about your pending nomination.

832
01:04:00,570 --> 01:04:05,371
My wife keeps telling me
it's a great leap for Southern women.

833
01:04:05,541 --> 01:04:06,769
Thank you.

834
01:04:07,710 --> 01:04:09,678
You're wondering
why I asked you here.

835
01:04:09,846 --> 01:04:12,906
Well, yeah.

836
01:04:13,082 --> 01:04:14,947
I hear you have family in Columbia.

837
01:04:15,118 --> 01:04:18,144
Yeah, my wife's sister
and some cousins.

838
01:04:18,321 --> 01:04:21,552
You've been inquiring about
transferring to the Columbia P.D.

839
01:04:21,724 --> 01:04:23,191
I know a lot of people.

840
01:04:23,359 --> 01:04:25,691
Some of whom may be able
to make that happen.

841
01:04:25,862 --> 01:04:28,956
Bypassing the usual
bureaucratic channels and such.

842
01:04:29,499 --> 01:04:31,296
Well, that would be...

843
01:04:33,703 --> 01:04:35,432
I would be much obliged.

844
01:04:36,272 --> 01:04:38,832
But in return
I need to ask something of you.

845
01:04:39,008 --> 01:04:43,206
- Off the record, do you understand?
- Yeah.

846
01:04:43,379 --> 01:04:47,713
I was hoping not to get involved in this,
but circumstances are such that...

847
01:04:49,118 --> 01:04:51,348
it seems unavoidable.

848
01:04:52,355 --> 01:04:55,950
I need you to tell me everything about
the Jay Burgess investigation.

849
01:04:56,793 --> 01:04:59,660
I know this is highly irregular...

850
01:04:59,829 --> 01:05:03,287
but I'm worried that someone
may be wrongfully blamed for this.

851
01:05:03,466 --> 01:05:05,934
And I can't let that happen again.

852
01:05:15,678 --> 01:05:17,270
He's home.

853
01:05:19,549 --> 01:05:21,915
Let's wait a minute,
see if a light comes on.

854
01:05:22,085 --> 01:05:24,781
I think I should be the one
to go talk to him.

855
01:05:27,623 --> 01:05:29,318
I've been thinking.

856
01:05:30,226 --> 01:05:33,525
You should really try and make
a transition to a bigger market.

857
01:05:33,696 --> 01:05:36,324
You're beautiful, you're smart.

858
01:05:36,499 --> 01:05:39,900
You're number one in Charleston,
but that's what? A few thousand?

859
01:05:40,069 --> 01:05:41,730
It's nothing.

860
01:05:41,904 --> 01:05:44,395
If you went national,
you'd be seen by millions.

861
01:05:45,208 --> 01:05:49,269
- I have had a couple of big offers.
- Really?

862
01:05:49,445 --> 01:05:51,208
- Yeah.
- So, what's the problem?

863
01:05:51,748 --> 01:05:54,911
Well, for one, in a big market
the competition's tougher...

864
01:05:55,084 --> 01:05:57,177
and the expectations are higher.

865
01:05:57,720 --> 01:06:01,247
- So what?
- So, what if I can't hack it?

866
01:06:02,558 --> 01:06:07,928
I mean, I don't have some
big, happy family to fall back on.

867
01:06:08,097 --> 01:06:12,193
My parents are dead
and there's nobody else.

868
01:06:12,368 --> 01:06:18,136
So if I take a big job and fail at it,
then how would I support myself?

869
01:06:18,708 --> 01:06:21,939
So your concern
is financial security?

870
01:06:22,678 --> 01:06:23,770
Well, yeah.

871
01:06:23,946 --> 01:06:26,278
- You'll have to be smart.
- Yeah.

872
01:06:26,449 --> 01:06:28,314
- And cautious.
- Exactly.

873
01:06:28,484 --> 01:06:30,213
- And gutless.
- What?

874
01:06:30,386 --> 01:06:32,286
I'm serious. No guts, no glory.

875
01:06:32,455 --> 01:06:35,947
You're not going for the glory,
so really, who needs the guts?

876
01:06:36,692 --> 01:06:38,284
Did you just insult me?

877
01:06:50,740 --> 01:06:53,834
It's almost 11:00 at night.
Where's he going?

878
01:06:54,010 --> 01:06:56,911
I don't know. Let's find out.

879
01:07:31,714 --> 01:07:34,182
- What is this?
- It's a gay club.

880
01:07:34,350 --> 01:07:35,544
Out here?

881
01:07:35,718 --> 01:07:38,209
You think
it's easy being gay in the South?

882
01:07:38,387 --> 01:07:40,719
Especially if you're a cop.

883
01:07:44,660 --> 01:07:45,718
- Hey.
- Hey.

884
01:07:45,895 --> 01:07:48,591
- Hey there.
- Hey, how's it going?

885
01:07:49,565 --> 01:07:51,556
Haven't seen you in a while.

886
01:07:51,734 --> 01:07:54,897
Hey, fellas. You don't mind
if I talk to my friend, do you?

887
01:07:55,071 --> 01:07:57,039
What are you doing here?
Following me?

888
01:07:57,206 --> 01:07:59,436
No, I'm not,
but we need to talk to you.

889
01:07:59,609 --> 01:08:01,236
Who's we?

890
01:08:01,711 --> 01:08:03,110
- Are you with her?
- Hi.

891
01:08:03,279 --> 01:08:06,043
Mr. Wickham, we were wondering
if you could help us.

892
01:08:06,215 --> 01:08:08,877
What exactly really happened
to your face?

893
01:08:09,051 --> 01:08:10,450
My face?

894
01:08:10,620 --> 01:08:12,884
Why? Raley knows I got into a fight.

895
01:08:13,055 --> 01:08:14,784
Nice story. Try again, Pat.

896
01:08:14,957 --> 01:08:18,984
Look, the truth always comes out.
Better if you just tell us now, talk to us.

897
01:08:20,663 --> 01:08:23,325
- Tell us about the police station fire.
- Screw off.

898
01:08:23,499 --> 01:08:27,094
- What about Hampton Park?
- Nobody knows about any of that.

899
01:08:27,270 --> 01:08:29,670
Just don't go there, please.

900
01:08:33,509 --> 01:08:34,874
Get down!

901
01:08:44,320 --> 01:08:46,447
Get in the car, get in the car.

902
01:09:02,805 --> 01:09:04,466
Go, go!

903
01:09:18,754 --> 01:09:20,244
Well, you're lucky.

904
01:09:20,423 --> 01:09:23,017
That bullet barely nicked you.

905
01:09:23,192 --> 01:09:26,525
- Yeah, well, it still hurts.
- I know.

906
01:09:29,932 --> 01:09:32,264
- Nice necklace.
- Thank you.

907
01:09:32,435 --> 01:09:36,394
- It doesn't exactly seem like your style.
- It's not.

908
01:09:36,572 --> 01:09:39,370
- Then why do you wear it?
- Sentimental.

909
01:09:39,542 --> 01:09:41,510
From your parents?

910
01:09:41,677 --> 01:09:44,373
- Old boyfriend?
- No.

911
01:09:44,547 --> 01:09:48,847
My bosses gave it to me after I won
number one three years in a row.

912
01:09:52,521 --> 01:09:54,648
- There you go.
- Thank you.

913
01:09:54,824 --> 01:09:56,416
You're welcome.

914
01:10:02,164 --> 01:10:05,759
- So I get it now.
- Get what?

915
01:10:05,935 --> 01:10:08,995
Why you'll never leave
your job at the station.

916
01:10:09,171 --> 01:10:11,639
Financial security my ass.

917
01:10:11,807 --> 01:10:14,970
You, my friend,
are seriously full of crap.

918
01:10:17,446 --> 01:10:22,645
So is that your version
of small talk or foreplay?

919
01:10:22,818 --> 01:10:24,445
I've seen you in action.

920
01:10:24,620 --> 01:10:27,987
With Louis Jones, Pat Jr.
You're a great interviewer.

921
01:10:28,524 --> 01:10:30,754
You could go anywhere
and be a star.

922
01:10:30,926 --> 01:10:33,827
Says the man
whose TV only gets three channels.

923
01:10:33,996 --> 01:10:35,327
But you won't.

924
01:10:35,498 --> 01:10:37,227
Because you need to stay.

925
01:10:37,400 --> 01:10:41,302
Your parents are all gone.
You avoid getting close to people.

926
01:10:41,470 --> 01:10:44,496
You'll never quit,
you'll never try something else...

927
01:10:44,673 --> 01:10:49,906
because your job is the one true
long-term relationship you've got.

928
01:11:17,506 --> 01:11:19,701
You look deep in thought.

929
01:11:21,544 --> 01:11:24,104
I was remembering when we met.

930
01:11:27,316 --> 01:11:30,945
God, you were so unattainable.

931
01:11:31,320 --> 01:11:33,720
Sailing high above
with the socialite crowd...

932
01:11:33,889 --> 01:11:36,687
barely knowing
peons like me even existed.

933
01:11:36,859 --> 01:11:40,420
When you agreed to marry me,
I couldn't believe it.

934
01:11:41,230 --> 01:11:43,255
And I couldn't figure out why.

935
01:11:44,266 --> 01:11:47,599
You were a hero, George.
Every girl wants a hero.

936
01:11:48,370 --> 01:11:50,634
And I fell in love with you.

937
01:11:56,045 --> 01:11:57,103
Are you still?

938
01:12:06,522 --> 01:12:11,016
The night you told me the truth
about the fire...

939
01:12:14,063 --> 01:12:15,792
something just changed.

940
01:12:15,965 --> 01:12:20,368
Everything that I thought you were and
everything I thought you could be...

941
01:12:20,536 --> 01:12:23,198
was based on a lie.

942
01:12:26,709 --> 01:12:29,143
And I felt betrayed.

943
01:12:35,851 --> 01:12:39,014
And I knew
I'd never let you betray me again.

944
01:12:43,926 --> 01:12:46,053
I'm sorry, George.

945
01:13:09,051 --> 01:13:11,849
- Hey, did you see this?
- What?

946
01:13:12,021 --> 01:13:14,717
Pat Jr's attack
happened five years ago.

947
01:13:14,890 --> 01:13:16,790
- September 14th.
- So?

948
01:13:16,959 --> 01:13:20,554
So the police station fire happened
five years ago, September 15th.

949
01:13:23,832 --> 01:13:25,459
Cleveland Jones was at both.

950
01:13:26,502 --> 01:13:28,129
Cleveland was a redneck.

951
01:13:28,304 --> 01:13:30,772
And rednecks aren't fond
of the gay population.

952
01:13:30,940 --> 01:13:34,376
And cops aren't too fond
of rednecks who beat up cops' kids.

953
01:13:35,177 --> 01:13:37,304
Do you think Pat Sr.
beat up Cleveland?

954
01:13:38,981 --> 01:13:42,747
Or George, or Jay, or all of them.

955
01:13:49,391 --> 01:13:52,758
Pat, please don't forget
to fix the stroller today.

956
01:13:53,896 --> 01:13:56,194
Oh, my God. Pat?

957
01:13:58,434 --> 01:14:00,902
They're here for me. It's all right.

958
01:14:06,742 --> 01:14:09,870
- Should I stay?
- I'm fine, honey.

959
01:14:10,713 --> 01:14:14,012
- Are you sure?
- Yeah, go ahead, it's okay.

960
01:14:18,821 --> 01:14:20,652
Are you gonna leave too?

961
01:14:22,258 --> 01:14:24,089
You guys wanna come in?

962
01:14:27,997 --> 01:14:30,056
I know why you ran.

963
01:14:32,368 --> 01:14:35,428
It must have been hard
living a lie all these years.

964
01:14:37,206 --> 01:14:39,640
It's not like I had a choice.

965
01:14:42,745 --> 01:14:47,011
My father and George used to tell
homo jokes around the dinner table.

966
01:14:47,182 --> 01:14:49,616
And I used to laugh along.

967
01:14:49,785 --> 01:14:54,848
And one day my dad caught me
in my bedroom with a friend.

968
01:14:55,024 --> 01:15:00,724
And if my mom hadn't stopped him,
I swear to God, he would've killed me.

969
01:15:01,196 --> 01:15:03,824
Secrets cost you a lot, huh?

970
01:15:04,466 --> 01:15:08,630
Your freedom, integrity,
even your face.

971
01:15:10,572 --> 01:15:14,440
Cleveland Jones did that, didn't he?
In the park.

972
01:15:14,910 --> 01:15:18,209
Him and two of his friends.

973
01:15:18,514 --> 01:15:21,915
They used the end of a bat
like a pile driver in my mouth.

974
01:15:23,485 --> 01:15:26,977
The surgeons
did the best they could but...

975
01:15:28,157 --> 01:15:30,284
Wasn't good enough for your dad,
was it?

976
01:15:32,127 --> 01:15:35,153
Yeah, maybe he still loved me.

977
01:15:37,132 --> 01:15:38,326
Maybe.

978
01:15:39,501 --> 01:15:41,162
He showed you some mug shots?

979
01:15:42,805 --> 01:15:45,205
Yeah, Cleveland
was the only one I recognized.

980
01:15:45,374 --> 01:15:47,706
What did he tell you
he was gonna do?

981
01:15:48,944 --> 01:15:53,904
He just said that he and his friends
were gonna take care of it.

982
01:15:55,384 --> 01:15:58,683
His friends?
You mean George and Jay.

983
01:15:58,854 --> 01:16:01,049
They didn't want me testifying
in a trial.

984
01:16:01,223 --> 01:16:05,284
So they just wanted to make sure
that Jones confessed.

985
01:16:05,461 --> 01:16:07,452
How did the police station
fire happen?

986
01:16:08,697 --> 01:16:10,562
I really don't know.

987
01:16:10,733 --> 01:16:15,864
I was in the hospital for weeks,
I was in pain, I was on meds.

988
01:16:17,005 --> 01:16:21,499
Anything that happened that night
no one ever talked to me about it.

989
01:16:22,144 --> 01:16:25,477
You never bothered to tell
anybody else about what you knew?

990
01:16:25,814 --> 01:16:29,545
They had gotten revenge for me
one way or another.

991
01:16:30,219 --> 01:16:34,087
I owed them something.
I owed them.

992
01:16:34,957 --> 01:16:37,517
And you just filled in one lie
for another, huh?

993
01:16:39,461 --> 01:16:40,485
Well...

994
01:16:42,331 --> 01:16:43,355
it's over now.

995
01:16:47,536 --> 01:16:50,994
What are you gonna do? You can't...

996
01:16:51,807 --> 01:16:55,334
Well, it's like she told you before.
The truth always comes out.

997
01:16:55,511 --> 01:16:57,502
All you have control over is how.

998
01:16:59,314 --> 01:17:00,508
Don't.

999
01:17:19,334 --> 01:17:23,031
- Thirty-eight years.
- Ma'am?

1000
01:17:23,405 --> 01:17:27,068
Thirty-eight years I've been dreaming
about making my name in the law.

1001
01:17:27,242 --> 01:17:29,574
Other girls
were playing Barbie and dress up.

1002
01:17:29,745 --> 01:17:32,407
I was pretending
to be Clarence Darrow or John Jay.

1003
01:17:32,815 --> 01:17:36,546
After tomorrow, I bet some little girl
will be pretending to be you.

1004
01:17:37,252 --> 01:17:38,617
Maybe.

1005
01:18:04,079 --> 01:18:08,106
<i>Pat Wickham Jr. shot twice
at close range late this afternoon.</i>

1006
01:18:08,283 --> 01:18:11,218
<i>Police are calling Britt Shelley
a person of interest.</i>

1007
01:18:11,386 --> 01:18:12,410
What?

1008
01:18:12,588 --> 01:18:17,582
<i>According to Wickham's wife, Shelley
was last seen with her husband.</i>

1009
01:18:17,759 --> 01:18:19,056
We gotta do something.

1010
01:18:20,362 --> 01:18:22,830
I've got an idea,
but we have to split up.

1011
01:18:23,966 --> 01:18:25,267
Okay.

1012
01:18:30,739 --> 01:18:34,072
- Press conference in 30 minutes.
- I'll be ready.

1013
01:18:34,910 --> 01:18:36,434
- Good luck, judge.
- Thank you.

1014
01:18:36,612 --> 01:18:37,670
This is it.

1015
01:18:42,918 --> 01:18:44,510
Miranda?

1016
01:18:54,229 --> 01:18:56,026
I knew you'd show up.

1017
01:19:00,102 --> 01:19:01,535
I'd go with the long ones.

1018
01:19:05,007 --> 01:19:06,634
My clerk let you in.

1019
01:19:06,808 --> 01:19:09,936
- Thank you for trusting me.
- I don't trust you.

1020
01:19:10,112 --> 01:19:13,843
I trust Raley, and he told me
you have a story to tell me.

1021
01:19:14,249 --> 01:19:16,240
I know who killed Jay Burgess...

1022
01:19:16,418 --> 01:19:18,978
Pat Wickham Jr.
and Cleveland Jones.

1023
01:19:20,622 --> 01:19:22,112
Please.

1024
01:19:24,293 --> 01:19:27,456
Believe it or not
I'm actually kind of relieved.

1025
01:19:27,629 --> 01:19:30,189
You need to come clean, George.

1026
01:19:30,766 --> 01:19:32,563
Yeah, I guess so.

1027
01:19:33,068 --> 01:19:37,471
Five years ago Cleveland Jones
attacked Pat Jr. in Hampton Park.

1028
01:19:37,639 --> 01:19:42,235
Pat Sr. wanted justice but he didn't
want his son's sexual orientation out.

1029
01:19:42,411 --> 01:19:44,971
So he and Jay pick Cleveland up.

1030
01:19:45,147 --> 01:19:48,207
The three of you were gonna beat
him until he confessed.

1031
01:19:49,184 --> 01:19:52,278
But things didn't go according to plan,
did they, George?

1032
01:19:52,454 --> 01:19:55,821
One of you,
doesn't really matter which...

1033
01:19:56,325 --> 01:19:59,158
bashed the kid's skull
until he was dead.

1034
01:19:59,561 --> 01:20:01,995
To cover their tracks,
the cops started a fire.

1035
01:20:02,397 --> 01:20:04,024
<i>Blaming Cleveland for it.</i>

1036
01:20:04,199 --> 01:20:07,862
Pretended to be victims themselves
and helped everyone get out.

1037
01:20:08,537 --> 01:20:11,529
- Became heroes.
- Yeah.

1038
01:20:12,207 --> 01:20:16,234
I guess everything
would've been fine if I just let it rest.

1039
01:20:16,411 --> 01:20:20,040
- But you couldn't, could you?
- No, I couldn't.

1040
01:20:20,215 --> 01:20:24,743
The cops knew the only way to avoid
being exposed was to shut Raley up.

1041
01:20:24,920 --> 01:20:26,012
One way or another.

1042
01:20:26,622 --> 01:20:28,021
The girl at the party.

1043
01:20:28,190 --> 01:20:32,354
And then you found Suzi Monroe and
you sent her to hit on me and drug me.

1044
01:20:32,794 --> 01:20:35,228
Done anything for a fix.
She'd hump the couch.

1045
01:20:35,397 --> 01:20:37,831
<i>And you made sure she OD'd.</i>

1046
01:20:39,468 --> 01:20:43,302
Yeah. We'd been around long enough.
We knew how it was done.

1047
01:20:43,705 --> 01:20:46,196
When Raley woke up,
they told him to keep quiet.

1048
01:20:46,375 --> 01:20:48,673
But Jay made sure
it became big news.

1049
01:20:48,844 --> 01:20:50,539
Jay and me.

1050
01:20:51,346 --> 01:20:56,079
My newscast distracted the public and
assured that Raley would lose his job.

1051
01:20:56,251 --> 01:21:00,381
Then Jay bribed the new
arson investigator to close the case.

1052
01:21:01,356 --> 01:21:07,420
- So if all this is true, who killed Jay?
- George did.

1053
01:21:08,697 --> 01:21:11,029
Pat Sr's death
really shook Jay up...

1054
01:21:11,199 --> 01:21:14,168
so Jay called George
and said he wanted to come clean.

1055
01:21:14,836 --> 01:21:16,963
But George couldn't let that happen.

1056
01:21:17,372 --> 01:21:22,139
<i>So he had Jay killed
and framed me for the murder.</i>

1057
01:21:26,348 --> 01:21:29,806
You're right about everything,
except the last part.

1058
01:21:30,118 --> 01:21:31,449
I didn't kill Jay.

1059
01:21:33,021 --> 01:21:37,117
Actually, I thought that you had
murdered him and Pat Jr. for revenge.

1060
01:21:37,726 --> 01:21:41,059
And that you came here today
to kill me.

1061
01:21:55,043 --> 01:21:58,877
I'm a good judge, Britt.
Maybe even a great judge.

1062
01:21:59,047 --> 01:22:00,810
So believe me when I tell you...

1063
01:22:00,982 --> 01:22:04,975
sometimes the end
really does justify the means.

1064
01:22:13,128 --> 01:22:14,595
No.

1065
01:22:22,571 --> 01:22:24,368
Oh, my God.

1066
01:22:25,674 --> 01:22:27,699
You were there, weren't you?

1067
01:22:31,480 --> 01:22:32,504
What's going on?

1068
01:22:32,948 --> 01:22:36,247
You hadn't just gotten to the station
when the fire happened.

1069
01:22:36,418 --> 01:22:39,649
You had been there for a while.
Watching the interrogation.

1070
01:22:41,890 --> 01:22:45,485
You were in the room when they killed
Cleveland Jones, weren't you?

1071
01:22:45,861 --> 01:22:49,194
Put the gun on the desk, face down
on the floor, now. Do it now!

1072
01:22:53,869 --> 01:22:56,531
- On the floor.
- You know every cop in the city.

1073
01:22:56,938 --> 01:22:58,064
Wait a minute.

1074
01:22:58,240 --> 01:23:01,607
But these guys, they're different.

1075
01:23:02,110 --> 01:23:04,237
<i>You and these guys go way back.</i>

1076
01:23:04,412 --> 01:23:07,677
You grew up together. Right?

1077
01:23:07,883 --> 01:23:09,783
That's why you wanted to be there...

1078
01:23:09,951 --> 01:23:12,977
when they interrogated the bastard
that hurt Pat's son.

1079
01:23:13,155 --> 01:23:15,214
Maybe you started
with good intentions.

1080
01:23:15,390 --> 01:23:18,757
Maybe you thought you'd just come
and prosecute him yourself.

1081
01:23:19,361 --> 01:23:22,797
But instead you stayed...

1082
01:23:22,964 --> 01:23:27,128
and watched Jay, George and Pat
pummel him to death.

1083
01:23:28,370 --> 01:23:33,637
<i>You knew that if Raley found out,
your career would be over.</i>

1084
01:23:33,809 --> 01:23:36,073
You couldn't let that happen.

1085
01:23:36,478 --> 01:23:38,912
So that's where the cover-up began.

1086
01:23:39,080 --> 01:23:40,445
<i>First it was Cleveland.</i>

1087
01:23:40,615 --> 01:23:43,482
<i>And then it was Suzi Monroe.</i>

1088
01:23:43,652 --> 01:23:45,711
<i>And then Jay.</i>

1089
01:23:47,255 --> 01:23:49,621
And now it's my turn, right?

1090
01:23:51,059 --> 01:23:54,460
Well, I'm impressed.

1091
01:23:54,629 --> 01:23:56,756
They say many
highly successful people...

1092
01:23:56,932 --> 01:24:00,595
are actually
functioning lying psychopaths.

1093
01:24:00,902 --> 01:24:03,803
You are so very convincing.

1094
01:24:03,972 --> 01:24:05,735
She sold me, that's for sure.

1095
01:24:07,776 --> 01:24:09,835
- Britt, you okay?
- Yeah.

1096
01:24:12,214 --> 01:24:15,274
You have been looking out
for someone all these years.

1097
01:24:15,450 --> 01:24:17,008
But it wasn't me, was it?

1098
01:24:24,926 --> 01:24:26,791
Let's go, judge.

1099
01:24:29,364 --> 01:24:31,457
- This all your handiwork?
- Get moving.

1100
01:24:31,633 --> 01:24:35,330
Yeah, I learned a few things about
hand-to-hand combat.

1101
01:24:36,705 --> 01:24:38,366
Thank God you're okay.

1102
01:24:38,907 --> 01:24:41,535
- Hey, come on.
- Just a second.

1103
01:24:45,480 --> 01:24:47,380
Okay, I'll let you know.

1104
01:24:48,416 --> 01:24:49,906
- Hi.
- Hi.

1105
01:24:50,085 --> 01:24:51,848
God, I'm starving. Who was that?

1106
01:24:52,020 --> 01:24:54,181
Fire chief.
Offered to give my job back.

1107
01:24:54,623 --> 01:24:58,286
- That's great.
- Yeah, well, let him stew for a while.

1108
01:24:59,794 --> 01:25:01,853
Crab sandwich.

1109
01:25:02,631 --> 01:25:06,192
- Meatball hero.
- Nice work.

1110
01:25:06,368 --> 01:25:08,529
So how did it go at the station?

1111
01:25:08,703 --> 01:25:11,001
Great.
They want me back at work too.

1112
01:25:11,773 --> 01:25:14,241
With a hefty raise
and hour-long specials...

1113
01:25:14,409 --> 01:25:16,741
new big office, my own assistant.

1114
01:25:17,512 --> 01:25:19,878
- That sounds like a good offer.
- Yeah, it is.

1115
01:25:20,048 --> 01:25:22,039
I told them
I wanted to think about it.

1116
01:25:22,217 --> 01:25:25,209
I wanna check out some
of the national networks first.

1117
01:25:25,387 --> 01:25:26,752
That's a great idea.

1118
01:25:26,922 --> 01:25:29,891
Yeah, well, don't get too excited.

1119
01:25:30,058 --> 01:25:33,926
I kind of just wanna explore
my possibilities, you know.

1120
01:25:34,095 --> 01:25:37,553
Maybe I don't need the Charleston
station so much anymore.

1121
01:25:37,732 --> 01:25:41,463
- At least as a long-term relationship.
- No?

1122
01:25:41,836 --> 01:25:43,770
So, what do you need?

1123
01:25:43,939 --> 01:25:49,104
Don't tell anybody, but I kinda have
a thing for clean-shaven firemen.

